    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d324-a1">

                <pb facs="0571" n="557" xml:id="pg557"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum for the Secretary of State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-02">October 2,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Under date of 9 September and 10 September we sent Ambassador Murphy two
                        reports<anchor n="20" xml:id="d324-f1"/> from our Bari office referring to
                    statements of Starker of Neubacher’s staff. Copies of these statements were sent
                    to Ambassador Harriman<anchor n="21" xml:id="d324-f2"/> and General
                        Deane,<anchor n="22" xml:id="d324-f3"/> who in turn showed them to the
                    Russians.</p>
                <p>You may find of significance that in a message from General Deane to us today, he
                    states that General Fitin<anchor n="23" xml:id="d324-f4"/> is grateful for the
                    information which was sent to him and requests that more information be
                    forwarded as it becomes available.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Donovan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d324-f1" n="20" xml:id="d324-f1-content">
                <p>Neither printed, but for the substance of these two reports, see telegrams 313,
                    September 7, 1 p.m., and 324, September 7, midnight, from Caserta, <ref
                        target="#pg549">p. 549</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d324-f2" n="21" xml:id="d324-f2-content">
                <p>W. Averell Harriman, American Ambassador in the Soviet Union.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d324-f3" n="22" xml:id="d324-f3-content">
                <p>Maj. Gen. John R. Deane, Head of the United States Military Mission in the Soviet
                    Union.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d324-f4" n="23" xml:id="d324-f4-content">
                <p>Lt. Gen. Pavel Mikhailovich Fitin, Head of Soviet External Intelligence
                    Services.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
